### Orbit.Api manual test requests.
### Works with Visual Studio's built-in .http endpoint explorer and VS Code's "REST Client" extension.
### Run against the Docker Compose stack (`docker compose up --build`) unless you change @baseUrl below.
###
### Deliberately short: one working example per resource, plus the checks that say something a unit
### test can't. Listing a resource again just to watch it appear is left out - the create response
### already carries the id, and the automated suite covers the round trip.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### Register a new account. Change the email/userName if you run this more than once - both are unique
### per account.
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "userName": "testuser",
  "displayName": "Test User",
  "password": "correct horse battery staple"
}

### Log in with the same credentials - emailOrUserName accepts either one. Copy the "token" value from
### the response into @token below (VS Code's REST Client can do this automatically via
### {{login.response.body.$.token}}; if your tool doesn't support that, paste it in by hand).
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "emailOrUserName": "testuser",
  "password": "correct horse battery staple"
}

### Everything below requires a token from register/login above.
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Without a token this returns 401 - worth running by hand, since it is the one thing that goes
### wrong silently: an endpoint mapped outside the authorized group serves everyone's data.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notes

### Create a note. Content is a list of lines rather than a string: each line is either plain text or a
### checklist item with its own checked state. isPrivate/encryptedContent are how a private note
### travels - the browser seals title and content into encryptedContent and sends both readable fields
### empty, so leave them as they are here unless you are testing that path.
# @name createNote
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "First note",
  "content": [
    { "text": "Created through requests.http", "isChecklistItem": false, "isChecked": false },
    { "text": "A checklist line", "isChecklistItem": true, "isChecked": false }
  ],
  "isPrivate": false,
  "encryptedContent": null
}

### Fetch it by id (VS Code's REST Client picks the id up via {{createNote.response.body.$}}; if your
### tool doesn't support that, paste it in by hand).
@noteId = {{createNote.response.body.$}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a task list. isCompleted on the task list itself is derived server-side from whether every
### item is completed, so it's ignored here even if you set it - see the "Tasks" section in README.md.
### Each item carries its own notification settings; "None" for both channels means it never notifies.
# @name createTaskList
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Groceries",
  "items": [
    {
      "description": "Buy milk",
      "dueDateUtc": "2026-08-20T18:00:00Z",
      "isCompleted": false,
      "linkedTaskListId": null,
      "overdueNotificationChannel": "None",
      "remindDaily": false,
      "dailyReminderNotificationChannel": "None",
      "dailyReminderTimeOfDay": "09:00:00"
    },
    {
      "description": "Buy bread",
      "dueDateUtc": null,
      "isCompleted": false,
      "linkedTaskListId": null,
      "overdueNotificationChannel": "None",
      "remindDaily": false,
      "dailyReminderNotificationChannel": "None",
      "dailyReminderTimeOfDay": "09:00:00"
    }
  ]
}

@taskListId = {{createTaskList.response.body.$}}

### Check off both items - isCompleted on the list itself should come back true.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskListId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Groceries",
  "items": [
    {
      "description": "Buy milk",
      "dueDateUtc": "2026-08-20T18:00:00Z",
      "isCompleted": true,
      "linkedTaskListId": null,
      "overdueNotificationChannel": "None",
      "remindDaily": false,
      "dailyReminderNotificationChannel": "None",
      "dailyReminderTimeOfDay": "09:00:00"
    },
    {
      "description": "Buy bread",
      "dueDateUtc": null,
      "isCompleted": true,
      "linkedTaskListId": null,
      "overdueNotificationChannel": "None",
      "remindDaily": false,
      "dailyReminderNotificationChannel": "None",
      "dailyReminderTimeOfDay": "09:00:00"
    }
  ]
}

### Fetch it again - isCompleted should now be true.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskListId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Notification settings. allowShareNotifications starts false: being told what was shared with you
### always appears in the feed, and this switch only adds a push or e-mail on top.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The notification feed itself - what the bell shows.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Liveness, as the container's HEALTHCHECK runs it: reports only whether the process answers, so a
### database that is down does not restart the API.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Readiness, with every dependency's own result in the body - the one to read when something is
### wrong. /health adds the configuration check on top, which reports missing SMTP or VAPID settings.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready
